          <p>
            A headlamp also makes it safer to deal with the jobs that come with an outage. Refuelling a generator, checking a sump pump, finding the main breaker or carrying a candle or heater safely are all easier with both hands free. Use the headlamp, not a phone torch, and save the phone battery for calls and news.
          </p>

          <p>
            Pair the headlamps with a lantern for the room and an <a href="/best-emergency-radio/">emergency radio</a> for updates, and the lighting side of an outage is covered. None of it is expensive, and all of it works better if it is already in a box you can find in the dark.
          </p>
